    "goal": "Find and repair the root cause of build_contour_tree (nova/equilibrium/contour_tree.py) violating the tree invariant on real meshes. The independent brute-force control in tests/test_contour_tree_brute_force.py (in this base, from run r-20261002T075725216430-ctta-end-to-end-brute-force) shows that on every persisted compact Solov'ev certificate mesh the tree reports 133-138 nodes, 255 edges and overflow true against an edge capacity of 255, where a contour tree needs node_count - edge_count == 1. The existing tree tests passed on synthetic fixtures, so first state why they did not see it. Measure before repairing: per fixture, the mesh vertex count (valid, wall, interior), the join-tree and split-tree arc counts, the number of critical vertices of the piecewise-linear field (maxima, minima, saddles, wall-contact joins), and the merged tree's node and edge counts. The counts decide the cause; one candidate (unverified) is that join and split arcs are both emitted rather than merged, which would give about 2(V-1) edges. Also say whether 133-138 nodes is right: a Solov'ev field has few critical points, so a node count near the vertex count means regular vertices are kept as nodes. The §2 contract is a contour tree of critical nodes, with node and edge capacities stated and overflow refused visibly.",
